\description{
Every feature that the National Weather Service Damage Assessment Toolkit (DAT) service held when it was queried on
2026-11-11, with every field the service gives, at full resolution, in the service's spatial reference (WGS 84, EPSG:4326),
unmodified. Nothing is simplified, generalized, rounded, snapped or filtered: no swath filter, no date filter, no feature dropped (features with
no date or an empty geometry are kept).
\itemize{
\item \code{dat_points}: damage points surveyed on the ground, 241,456 features (the "Damage Points" layer).
\item \code{dat_lines}: centerlines of surveyed tornado tracks, 13,021 features (the "Damage Lines" layer).
\item \code{dat_polygons}: damage polygons, rated by EF scale, 11,172 features (the "Damage Polygons" layer); damage polygons of different EF
ratings are nested, so they overlap.
}
